# Design and Develop Custom Application (Mini Project) using Salesforce Cloud

## Aim
To design and develop a custom mini project application using Salesforce Cloud for managing a Student Library Management System.

---

# Software Requirements
- Internet Connection
- Web Browser (Chrome / Edge / Firefox)
- Salesforce Developer Account

---

# Theory
Salesforce is a cloud-based CRM platform used for developing scalable business applications.

Custom Objects in Salesforce allow users to create database tables according to application requirements. These objects can contain fields, tabs, records, and relationships.

In this practical, a custom application named **Library Management System** is created using:
- Custom Objects
- Custom Fields
- Tabs
- Lightning Application

---

# Mini Project Title
## Student Library Management System

---

# Steps to Perform the Practical

# Step 1: Create Salesforce Developer Account

1. Open the Salesforce Developer Signup page:
   https://developer.salesforce.com/signup

2. Fill in the required details:
   - Name
   - Email
   - Username
   - Company Name

3. Verify your email and log in to Salesforce.

---

# Step 2: Create Custom Objects

1. On Salesforce Dashboard click:
   - Setup
   - Object Manager

2. Click on:
```text
Create → Custom Object
```

3. Fill the details for the first object.

## Object 1: Book

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Label | Book |
| Plural Label | Books |
| Description | Stores information about books |

4. Click:
```text
Save & New
```

---

## Object 2: Student

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Label | Student |
| Plural Label | Students |
| Description | Stores information about students |

5. Click:
```text
Save
```

6. Newly created objects will appear in Object Manager.

---

# Step 3: Add Fields to Book Object

1. Go to:
```text
Object Manager → Book
```

2. Click:
```text
Fields & Relationships → New
```

3. Select:
```text
Text
```

4. Click:
```text
Next
```

